### Intelligent Customer Support System — sample requests
### Open in the VS Code "REST Client" extension or the JetBrains HTTP client.

@base = http://localhost:3000

### Health check
GET {{base}}/health

### Create a ticket (no classification)
POST {{base}}/tickets
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customer_id": "CUST-1001",
  "customer_email": "ann.adler@example.com",
  "customer_name": "Ann Adler",
  "subject": "Question about my subscription",
  "description": "I have a general question about how subscription billing works."
}

### Create a ticket WITH auto-classification
POST {{base}}/tickets?autoClassify=true
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customer_id": "CUST-1002",
  "customer_email": "ben.cole@example.com",
  "customer_name": "Ben Cole",
  "subject": "Cannot access my account",
  "description": "I cannot access my account, this is critical and production is down."
}

### Bulk import (JSON) with auto-classification
POST {{base}}/tickets/import?autoClassify=true
Content-Type: application/json

< ./sample-data.json

### List all tickets (paginated)
GET {{base}}/tickets?page=1&limit=10

### Filter: combined category + priority
GET {{base}}/tickets?category=account_access&priority=urgent

### Filter: full-text search
GET {{base}}/tickets?search=refund

### Get one ticket — replace :id with a real id from a create/list response
GET {{base}}/tickets/REPLACE_WITH_TICKET_ID

### Update a ticket
PUT {{base}}/tickets/REPLACE_WITH_TICKET_ID
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "in_progress",
  "assigned_to": "agent-7"
}

### Auto-classify an existing ticket
POST {{base}}/tickets/REPLACE_WITH_TICKET_ID/auto-classify

### Manual classification override
POST {{base}}/tickets/REPLACE_WITH_TICKET_ID/auto-classify
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "category": "billing_question",
  "priority": "high"
}

### Delete a ticket
DELETE {{base}}/tickets/REPLACE_WITH_TICKET_ID

### Validation error example (expect 400)
POST {{base}}/tickets
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customer_email": "not-an-email",
  "subject": "x"
}
